From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] pthread_mutex: declare _os_xbs_chrooted

pthread_mutex.c reads _os_xbs_chrooted, which libsystem_kernel defines in
wrappers/_libkernel_init.c, but no published header declares it: Apple's
build takes the declaration from an internal header. Declare it where it is
used.

Rebase-risk: low (one declaration).
---
diff --git a/src/pthread_mutex.c b/src/pthread_mutex.c
--- a/src/pthread_mutex.c
+++ b/src/pthread_mutex.c
@@ -53,6 +53,10 @@
 #include "resolver.h"
 #include "internal.h"
 #include "kern/kern_trace.h"
+
+// Set by libsystem_kernel (_libkernel_init.c) when running chrooted in a build
+// environment; Apple declares it in an unpublished header.
+extern bool _os_xbs_chrooted;
 
 #ifndef BUILDING_VARIANT /* [ */
 
